aption":"Panther Cave","poi_name":"","subject":"MCC  Gang","author":"John Duke","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3696","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3696"}},{"id":"3697","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4507","description":"You can paddle right through this mini cave just below Panther cave","caption":"Below Panther","poi_name":"","subject":"Amy","author":"John Duke","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3697","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3697"}},{"id":"3695","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4508","description":"Dave is runnin a class 2,a couple of miles above rt.11","caption":"Lower Cedar Creek","poi_name":"","subject":"Dave Cooke","author":"John Duke","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3695","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3695"}}],"detail":{"id":"1914","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Cedar Creek is a classic VA novice trip with some mild Class II rapids scattered along its length. The Lower Cedar Creek reach is somewhat more interesting than the upper two reaches, as it has slightly bigger rapids and some scenic features such as caves and a waterfall or two.\n\nThis is the usual run that includes most of what's interesting on Cedar Creek.  It is a 10.6 mile run from the Middle Rd bridge to US 11.  There are some travertine outcrops just upstream from the Middle Rd. bridge that can be explored by easily paddling a short distance upstream.  Keep in mind that although this is a pretty mellow river, the 10.6 mile run from Middle Rd bridge to US 11 can seem a long way to go, so give yourself plenty of daylight.\n\nThe takeout at Rt. 11 provides ample parking (this has changed) and a chance to check some differing RC gauges as described in the flow link.\n\nThere is a low water bridge about a mile above Rt. 11 that creates a Class II rapid and which can be run right. The best rapids on the river are located here and right below.\n\nOn a recent trip there was an incredible profusion of Virginia Bluebells. There are also a series of scenic cliffs that dominate most of river left and sometimes on the right. These cliffs are full of caves, including short one that you can paddle through.\n\nSee Also:\n\n_Classic Virginia Rivers,_ Ed Grove (1992 ed), p. 144.\n\n_Virginia Whitewater_, Roger Corbett (2000 ed.), p. 79.\n\n_Exploring Virginia's Waterways_, Ed Gertler (2022 ed.), p. 25.","averageGradient":"11","maxGradient":null,"length":"11","correlations":[{"reachID":"1914","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":"200 is open canoe","mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"200","beginMediumRunnable":"440","beginHighRunnable":"1600","endHighRunnable":"2400"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"CEDAR CREEK NEAR WINCHESTER, VA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01634500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"20","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.85","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"39.0812176","longitude":"-78.3294486"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/01634500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/01634500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"20","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs